# MusiX needs no environment variables to run.
#
# The web app has no server, no API keys and no accounts — it reads your music
# from disk and stores everything in your browser. `npm run dev` is enough.
#
# The variables below configure the *optional* local stem-separation service in
# backend/. They are read by the Python process, not by the web app, and every
# one has a sensible default.

# Where separated stems and uploads are kept.
# MUSIX_STORAGE=./backend/storage

# Where downloaded songs are saved. Defaults to <storage>/downloads, and can
# also be changed in Settings. Setting it here pins the folder and disables
# the Settings control.
# MUSIX_DOWNLOAD_DIR=C:\Users\You\Music\MusiX

# Largest file the service will accept, in bytes. Default: 512 MB.
# MUSIX_MAX_UPLOAD=536870912

# Demucs model. `htdemucs` gives vocals/drums/bass/other;
# `htdemucs_6s` adds guitar and piano and is roughly twice as slow.
# Asking for guitar or piano switches to the six-stem model automatically.
# MUSIX_MODEL=htdemucs

# Force a device. Left unset, CUDA is used when it is genuinely available.
# MUSIX_DEVICE=cpu

# Where the service listens. Keep it on the loopback address: it holds your
# audio, and nothing outside this machine should reach it.
# MUSIX_HOST=127.0.0.1
# MUSIX_PORT=8000

# Origins allowed to call the service, comma-separated.
# Defaults cover the Vite dev server and `npm run preview`.
# MUSIX_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=http://localhost:5173,http://127.0.0.1:5173
